{"name":"Brick Fence","hex":"#b38070","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"},{"term":"fence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin artificial barrier that separates two pieces of land or forms a perimeter enclosing the lands of a house, building, etc.","Someone who hides or buys and sells stolen goods, a criminal middleman for transactions of stolen goods."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose, contain or separate by building fence.","To defend or guard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"},{"title":"Fence","blocks":[{"text":"A fence is a structure that encloses an area, typically outdoors creating a boundary, and is usually constructed from posts that are connected by boards, wire, rails or netting. A fence differs from a wall in not having a solid foundation along its whole length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Westtown.jpg/330px-Westtown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.